---
import { SITE } from '../config/site';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Privacy"
  description={`How ${SITE.name} handles your data.`}
  crumbs={[['Privacy', '/privacy/']]}
>
  <h1>Privacy</h1>
  <h2>What you type into the calculators</h2>
  <p>The numbers you enter stay in your browser. They are not sent to us or stored.</p>
  <p>
    If you use “Copy link” in the savings planner, the link itself contains the energy numbers you
    entered (state, kWh, prices, appliance schedules and heating choice), never a bill amount.
    Anyone you send it to can read them, and when the link is opened the address reaches our host
    like any page request. We do not keep a copy.
  </p>
  <h2>Visit counts</h2>
  <p>
    To learn which pages are useful, each page sends us a few anonymous signals: the page address
    (for example /electricity-rates/ohio/), what kind of thing happened (a page view, a calculator
    used, a result shown, a form error, a scenario added, a share or download button used, or a tool
    opened from the home page), a broad category for how you arrived (search engine, AI assistant,
    social site, another website, a link on this site, or directly), and whether the browser is
    automated. We add these up into daily totals. None of the numbers you typed are included.
  </p>
  <p>
    We do not store your IP address, browser details, the exact page you came from, or anything else
    that could identify you, and we do not use cookies or local storage, so there is nothing to
    consent to and nothing that follows you between visits or sites.
  </p>
  <h2>Advertising and other services</h2>
  <p>
    This site currently has no advertising and no third-party scripts. If that changes, this page
    will say so first. The site is hosted on Cloudflare, which processes requests to deliver the
    pages.
  </p>
  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    <a href={`mailto:${SITE.contactEmail}`}>{SITE.contactEmail}</a>
  </p>
</Base>
